  "_commit": {
    "id": "b7352b3c9a3e01ea6aa9b2d81f4c4495bf4ccc98",
    "author": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "committer": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "message": "1.99.59: testCorrelation(), the correlation between a fit's tests; $conditionInformation\n\ntestCorrelation(x, method = c(\"cr2\", \"permutation\")) estimates the correlation between every two pairs' tests from\none fit (two conditions, one radius or k, unadjusted, CR2). Each patient's summary and weight are rebuilt from\n$pairwiseAssoc, $imageWeights and the new $conditionInformation (each condition's information per pair, the\nexcess_test's group totals S_g; ExcessResult::group_weight and PairTests::group_weight in the core). \"cr2\": the\ncross-products of the CR2 influences (squares sum to se^2). \"permutation\": conditions permuted over patients\n(SplitMix64, fixed seed, the same in Python), each test recomputed in closed form as excess_test does, correlation\nof the signed z. Computed in the core (test_correlation); the front end checks the rebuilt difference and se against\nthe table and refuses otherwise. SplitMix64 moves from multiradius.cpp to stats.hpp (unchanged). kontextualEngine()\nalso returns $variance. Every existing element and result is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0138g2RrJpkKQrMJF3k37EfW\n",
    "time": 1795134140
  },
